    "bottomLine": "The fastest way to remove the dark marks mold leaves behind, used after a real mold killer rather than instead of one.",
    "description": "RMR-86 is the product people buy after seeing a video of black stains vanishing from a wall in seconds, and on staining it really is fast. What makes RMR worth recommending is its honesty about what the product is. Its own FAQ answers the question directly: this product does not kill mold, it only removes the stains caused by mold and mildew. That makes RMR-86 a cleanup step, not a treatment. The safety data sheet lists sodium hypochlorite at 1 to 5 percent, which explains both the speed and the strong chlorine odor. Directions are simple: spray from 6 to 8 inches until the area is covered, let it work for at least 15 seconds, and rinse once the stains have gone. RMR lists decks, wood, vinyl, siding, drywall, concrete and brick as suitable, and warns against metals and fabrics because of the bleaching effect. Take the protective equipment seriously. RMR recommends a full face respirator with appropriate cartridges, a chemical suit and nitrile gloves, and you should ventilate the space and never mix it with other cleaners. Use it after RMR-141 or another registered fungicide has done the killing, on surfaces that will not be damaged by bleach."
