        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I stop mold from coming back?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Fix the moisture. Keep indoor humidity below 60 percent and ideally 30 to 50, run bathroom fans after showers, repair leaks quickly and dry wet materials within 24 to 48 hours. An inhibitor such as Concrobium Mold Control can help on surfaces prone to dampness, but humidity control does most of the work."
          }
