          The best mold remover depends on the job, because the products on the shelf do three different things. Some kill mold, some remove the stains it leaves, and some help stop it coming back. A bleach spray is the right tool for black mildew in shower grout and the wrong one for a basement wall, where it whitens the stain and leaves growth behind. Pick by surface and job, read the label for the EPA registration and contact time, and fix the moisture first, because no spray beats a damp wall.
